project descends from, `proxy/wsproxy.js`, carries a header reading
`MIT license`. Both statements were present upstream from the start.

In 2020, @neverbot's `maldorne/mud-web-proxy` added a `LICENSE.md` (commit
`2b1acf7`, "feat: license and readme files") stating GPL version 3 or later
and naming both copyright holders.

An earlier revision of this file said @neverbot had relicensed @plamzi's
MIT-headered code as GPL. That was wrong, and @neverbot corrected it in review
of PR #42: the GPL was already present in @plamzi's repository, so the 2020
`LICENSE.md` restated existing terms rather than imposing new ones. The
correction is recorded here rather than silently applied, because the original
claim was published and attributed conduct to a named person that did not
occur.

